{"root":"pli/ms","translators":["sujato"],"title":"Fords: a past life story","html":"<article id='ja25'><header><ul><li class='division'><span class='root'>Jātaka </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Stories of Past Lives 25 </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Ekakanipāta </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>The Book of the Ones </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Kuruṅgavagga </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>The Four-horned Antelope </span></li></ul>\n<h1 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>5. Titthajātaka </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Fords: a past life story </span></h1></header>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>“Aññamaññehi titthehi, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>At one ford or another </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>assaṁ pāyehi sārathi; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>lead the horse to drink, rider. </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Accāsanassa puriso, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>For man who overeats, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>pāyāsassapi tappatī”ti. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>even milk-rice is a torment. </span></span></p></blockquote>\n<p class='endsutta'><span class='root'>Titthajātakaṁ pañcamaṁ. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></p></article>"}
